target:    tests/fp-negative/scenarios.php
gate:      composer test:fp-negative-linux no-python3
kind:      restore-defect
expect:    missing: command not found
rationale: NOT A REGISTRY ENTRY, for the same structural reason as its neighbour: the gate needs
           a container. `composer test:mutations` runs on the developer's host, and on macOS
           /bin/sh is bash — under which the restored defect is INVISIBLE, because bash's
           "sh: python3: command not found" CONTAINS the reverted needle. Run there, this
           mutation reports SURVIVED on a correct tree. The gate above containerises, so its
           verdict does not depend on the host: measured both ways, the gate exits 1 under dash
           and 0 under bash.

           WHAT IT PROVES. That `no-python3`'s CONTROL 3 assertion still binds to the shell's raw
           answer reaching the detail line, on the shell CI actually runs. Restoring
           'command not found' is the defect introduced by 3dff4b9d, which kept free's Tier 1
           lane red on every push for a week while the export-fidelity gate itself was healthy —
           `baseline` passed in the same CI run that failed. See PITFALLS 93.

           WHY THIS DIFF AND NOT A DELETION. Deleting the needle also turns the scenario red, but
           it pins the wrong thing — that SOME needle is present. Nobody deletes an assertion;
           they write the one that is true of the machine in front of them. The one-literal
           revert is the mistake in its original shape.

           NOT AUTOMATED, and named so it is not mistaken for a lane. Nothing applies this file:
           `mutation-registry-test.php`'s loose loop validates its FORMAT only, and `FP_MUTATIONS`
           in run-rollup-floor.sh cannot host it — that lane executes its precondition as MySQL
           and hardcodes both the gate and the kill string. Applied and observed red by hand at
           Run 62. No `precondition:` header: the earlier draft carried one asserting "/bin/sh
           here is dash", which no runner evaluates — the gate now guarantees it instead.
---
diff --git a/tests/fp-negative/scenarios.php b/tests/fp-negative/scenarios.php
index 1ad3f17..b0cea20 100644
--- a/tests/fp-negative/scenarios.php
+++ b/tests/fp-negative/scenarios.php
@@ -178,7 +178,7 @@ function slimstat_neg_scenarios()
                 // found"). Lowercase 'not found' is the only wording common to both, and strpos
                 // is case-sensitive, so it cannot match the subject's own NOT-FOUND markers.
                 // PITFALLS 93. Pinned by tests/docker/mutations/A1-shell-wording-bash-only-01.
-                'not found',
+                'command not found',
                 'tables-read=0',
                 'the Python reader returned no fingerprint',
             ],
